---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={"Sound Design and Sampling — Auspicious Music"}
  description={"Sampling, synthesis and building playable instruments, documented with the audio each technique produced."}
  canonicalPath={"/sound-design/"}
  lang={"en"}
  noindex={false}
  loadStringField={false}
>
<Fragment slot="head">
<style is:global>
@layer components {
  .hub-head { padding-block: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem) clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4rem); }
  .hub-head h1 { max-width: 17ch; margin-top: 1.25rem; }
  .hub-head .lede { margin-top: 1.5rem; max-width: 58ch; }

  /* ---- hub signature ----
     Each hub opens on a diagram of its own discipline, so the five main
     sections stop reading as one template with different words. Line work
     only, one ember mark per figure, and hidden below 820px where the head
     needs its full width for type. */
  .hub-head__inner { display: grid; gap: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.5rem); align-items: center; }
  @media (min-width: 820px) {
    .hub-head__inner { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 0.62fr); }
  }
  .sig { display: none; }
  @media (min-width: 820px) {
    .sig { display: grid; gap: 0.875rem; justify-items: end; }
    .sig svg { inline-size: 100%; max-inline-size: 320px; height: auto; }
    .sig rect, .sig circle { fill: var(--line-strong); }
    .sig path, .sig line { stroke: var(--line-strong); stroke-width: 1.25; }
    .sig .sig-empty { fill: none; stroke: var(--line); stroke-width: 1; }
    .sig .sig-solid { fill: var(--ink-soft); }
    .sig .sig-mark { fill: var(--ember-bright); }
    circle.sig-mark { fill: none; stroke: var(--ember-bright); stroke-width: 2; }
    .sig .sig-play { stroke: var(--ember-bright); stroke-width: 1.25; }
    .sig figcaption {
      font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--t-meta);
      letter-spacing: var(--tr-meta); color: var(--muted);
    }
  }

  .topics { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .topics li { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .topics a {
    display: grid; gap: 0.375rem 2.5rem; padding-block: 1.5rem;
    text-decoration: none; align-items: baseline;
    transition: background-color var(--dur-fast) var(--ease);
  }
  .topics a:hover { background: var(--surface); }
  .topics h3 { font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 1.05rem + 0.75vw, 1.625rem); letter-spacing: -0.015em; }
  .topics p { color: var(--muted); font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.6; max-width: 58ch; }
  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .topics a { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 14rem) minmax(0, 1fr); align-items: start; }
  }

  .feature__inner { display: grid; gap: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.5rem); align-items: center; }
  @media (min-width: 940px) { .feature__inner { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1.15fr); } }
  .feature h2 { font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 1.15rem + 2.1vw, 2.75rem); max-width: 20ch; margin-top: 0.875rem; }
  .feature p { color: var(--dark-muted); margin-top: 1.125rem; max-width: 46ch; font-size: 1.0625rem; line-height: 1.65; }
  .feature .meta { margin-top: 1.5rem; }
  .feature .link { margin-top: 1.75rem; }
  .feature .ph { aspect-ratio: 4 / 3; }

  .tail { display: grid; gap: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4rem); }
  @media (min-width: 900px) { .tail { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.3fr) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 4.5rem; } }
  .glossary > div { padding-block: 1.125rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .glossary > div:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .glossary dt { font-weight: 550; font-size: 1.0625rem; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  .glossary dd { color: var(--muted); font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.6; margin-top: 0.25rem; max-width: 54ch; }
  .related li { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .related li:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .related a {
    display: flex; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1.5rem;
    padding-block: 1.125rem; text-decoration: none; font-size: 1.0625rem; font-weight: 500;
  }
  .related a:hover { color: var(--accent); }
  .related svg { width: 14px; height: 14px; flex: none; }
}
</style>
</Fragment>

<main id="content">

  <section class="hub-head" data-od-id="hub-head">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="hub-head__inner">
        <div>
        <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
          <ol>
            <li><a href="/">Home</a></li>
            <li>Sound Design</li>
          </ol>
        </nav>
        <h1>Sound design and sampling</h1>
        <p class="lede">Making a sound rather than choosing one. Sampling, synthesis and instrument building, each written up with the settings that produced the result and the points where it stopped behaving. Where audio is relevant, it is recorded for the guide rather than borrowed.</p>
      </div>
        <figure class="sig" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 200 118" fill="none" role="presentation"><rect x="0" y="104" width="4" height="8" rx="1"/><rect x="7" y="98" width="4" height="14" rx="1"/><rect x="14" y="90" width="4" height="22" rx="1"/><rect x="21" y="78" width="4" height="34" rx="1"/><rect x="28" y="60" width="4" height="52" rx="1"/><rect x="35" y="41" width="4" height="71" rx="1"/><rect x="42" y="24" width="4" height="88" rx="1"/><rect x="49" y="8" width="4" height="104" rx="1" class="sig-mark"/><rect x="56" y="20" width="4" height="92" rx="1"/><rect x="63" y="38" width="4" height="74" rx="1"/><rect x="70" y="51" width="4" height="61" rx="1"/><rect x="77" y="57" width="4" height="55" rx="1"/><rect x="84" y="49" width="4" height="63" rx="1"/><rect x="91" y="34" width="4" height="78" rx="1"/><rect x="98" y="46" width="4" height="66" rx="1"/><rect x="105" y="64" width="4" height="48" rx="1"/><rect x="112" y="74" width="4" height="38" rx="1"/><rect x="119" y="68" width="4" height="44" rx="1"/><rect x="126" y="60" width="4" height="52" rx="1"/><rect x="133" y="71" width="4" height="41" rx="1"/><rect x="140" y="82" width="4" height="30" rx="1"/><rect x="147" y="88" width="4" height="24" rx="1"/><rect x="154" y="93" width="4" height="19" rx="1"/><rect x="161" y="97" width="4" height="15" rx="1"/><rect x="168" y="100" width="4" height="12" rx="1"/><rect x="175" y="103" width="4" height="9" rx="1"/><rect x="182" y="105" width="4" height="7" rx="1"/><rect x="189" y="107" width="4" height="5" rx="1"/></svg>
          <figcaption>Spectrum</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section data-od-id="hub-topics" aria-labelledby="topics-title">
    <div class="shell">
      <h2 id="topics-title" style="position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip-path:inset(50%)">Topics in this hub</h2>
      <ul class="topics" data-reveal-group>
        <li data-reveal><a href="/publishing-roadmap/">
          <h3>Sampling</h3>
          <p>Recording, trimming, looping and the naming discipline that decides how painful the mapping stage is.</p>
        </a></li>
        <li data-reveal><a href="/sound-design/sampled-instruments/building-a-sampled-instrument/">
          <h3>Sampled instruments</h3>
          <p>Turning a folder of recordings into something that plays like an instrument rather than a sound effect.</p>
        </a></li>
        <li data-reveal><a href="/publishing-roadmap/">
          <h3>Synthesis</h3>
          <p>Subtractive, FM and noise-based design, approached through the sound you want rather than the theory.</p>
        </a></li>
        <li data-reveal><a href="/publishing-roadmap/">
          <h3>Transitions</h3>
          <p>Risers, falls and impacts built from the material already in the track.</p>
        </a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band band-dark feature" data-od-id="hub-feature" aria-labelledby="feature-title">
    <div class="shell feature__inner">
      <div class="ph" data-reveal>
        <span class="ph__label"><strong>Screenshot</strong> — Sampler zone editor, three velocity layers<br>to be captured at 2560 × 1440</span>
      </div>
      <div data-reveal data-reveal-delay="120">
        <p class="kicker">Lab — tested build</p>
        <h2 id="feature-title">How to Build a Sampled Instrument in Ableton Live</h2>
        <p>A viola recorded across three dynamic layers, trimmed and looped, then mapped into Sampler. The whole chain, including the two points where round-robin stopped behaving and what fixed it.</p>
        <p class="meta"><span>Ableton Live 12</span><span>Sampler</span><span>22 min</span></p>
        <a class="link" href="/sound-design/sampled-instruments/building-a-sampled-instrument/">Read the build
          <svg viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 7h10M8 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band" data-od-id="hub-latest" aria-labelledby="latest-title">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2 id="latest-title">Latest in Sound Design</h2>
        <p>Newest first. Every technique is written up with the audio it produced.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="index" data-reveal-group>
        <li data-reveal><a href="/sound-design/sampled-instruments/building-a-sampled-instrument/">
          <time class="index__date" datetime="2026-08-04">04 Aug 2026</time>
          <div>
            <h3>How to Build a Sampled Instrument in Ableton Live</h3>
            <p>Recording, trimming, looping and mapping a viola into Sampler — with the round-robin problems left in.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="index__tail"><span class="index__topic">Live 12 · 22 min</span></div>
        </a></li>
        <li data-reveal><a href="/publishing-roadmap/">
          <time class="index__date" datetime="2026-07-15">15 Jul 2026</time>
          <div>
            <h3>Designing Noise Risers Without a Dedicated Plug-in</h3>
            <p>Three transitions built from a single noise source and the stock devices already in the set.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="index__tail"><span class="index__topic">Live 12 · 10 min</span></div>
        </a></li>
        <li data-reveal><a href="/publishing-roadmap/">
          <time class="index__date" datetime="2026-06-30">30 Jun 2026</time>
          <div>
            <h3>Sampling Electric Guitar for a Playable Instrument</h3>
            <p>Where to sample, how far apart, and why the pick position matters more than the microphone.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="index__tail"><span class="index__topic">Live 12 · 15 min</span></div>
        </a></li>
        <li data-reveal><a href="/publishing-roadmap/">
          <time class="index__date" datetime="2026-06-08">08 Jun 2026</time>
          <div>
            <h3>Loop Points That Do Not Sound Looped</h3>
            <p>Zero crossings remove the click. Making the repetition inaudible is a different problem.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="index__tail"><span class="index__topic">Any sampler · 8 min</span></div>
        </a></li>
        <li data-reveal><a href="/publishing-roadmap/">
          <time class="index__date" datetime="2026-05-19">19 May 2026</time>
          <div>
            <h3>Reading a Spectrum Analyser Honestly</h3>
            <p>What the display is actually telling you, and the four ways it routinely misleads.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="index__tail"><span class="index__topic">Method · 12 min</span></div>
        </a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band band--tight band-surface" data-od-id="hub-tail">
    <div class="shell tail">
      <div>
        <h2 style="font-size:var(--t-h3);margin-bottom:1.5rem">Terms used across this hub</h2>
        <dl class="glossary">
          <div>
            <dt>Round-robin</dt>
            <dd>Cycling through several recordings of the same note so repeated notes do not sound identical.</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Velocity layer</dt>
            <dd>A separate recording used across a range of playing strengths, so dynamics change timbre and not just volume.</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Zero crossing</dt>
            <dd>The point where a waveform passes through silence — cutting there avoids the click a mid-waveform edit produces.</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Formant</dt>
            <dd>The resonance that gives a source its character. Transposing a sample too far moves it, which is why a repitched voice sounds artificial.</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 style="font-size:var(--t-h3);margin-bottom:1.5rem">Related</h2>
        <ul class="related">
          <li><a href="/ableton/">Ableton
            <svg viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 7h10M8 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a></li>
          <li><a href="/recording/">Recording
            <svg viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 7h10M8 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a></li>
          <li><a href="/resources/tools/sample-pitch/">Sample Pitch & Rate calculator
            <svg viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 7h10M8 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a></li>
          <li><a href="/legacy/the-spy-guitar/">The Spy Guitar (archive)
            <svg viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 7h10M8 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section data-od-id="relaunch-notice">
    <div class="shell relaunch">
      <p>Auspicious Music was relaunched under new ownership in 2026. Historical
         references are preserved for context.</p>
      <a class="link" href="/about/history-and-relaunch/">Read the history and relaunch note
        <svg viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 7h10M8 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

</main>
</BaseLayout>